  CONCLUSION Fluoxetine was superior to placebo in the acute phase treatment of major depressive disorder in child and  
  adolescent outpatients with severe, persistent depression. Complete remission of symptoms was rare."},                
  {"study_index": 3, "title": "Double‐blind placebo‐controlled study of nortriptyline in depressed adolescents using a  
  \\"fixed plasma level\\" design", "abstract": "We performed a random assignment, double-blind, placebo-controlled     
  study of nortriptyline (NT) in postpubertal 12- to 17-year-olds with Research Diagnostic Criteria (RDC) and DSM-III   
  major depressive disorder. The protocol included a 2-week placebo washout phase and an 8-week double-blind,           
